Cell["\<\
Answer: Z/2 x Z/4, Z/4 x Z/4, Z/6 x Z/6, Z/4 x Z/8; in each case m divides p \
- 1.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d451fc99-4d24-4edb-86e1-d2759e054c82"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Exercise 5.10", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"fcbe44f1-8bd8-4a24-8589-9485e4c15752"],

Cell["\<\
(c), (d) Over F_3 and F_2 a curve is supersingular when a = q + 1 - #E is \
divisible by p. For example y^2 = x^3 - x over F_3 has 4 points \
(supersingular) and y^2 + y = x^3 over F_2 has 3 points (supersingular), \
while y^2 + xy = x^3 + 1 over F_2 has 4 points (ordinary).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"06933367-31f4-405d-8ffa-96c2791623b9"],

