Cell["Chapter VIII - Elliptic Curves over Global Fields", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e937a7ff-bb2c-46af-9e8f-fc0ae3359a6e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Example (7.4)", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5da8822d-70f5-40c8-88c8-806047f0a669"],

Cell["\<\
E : y^2 = x^3 - 43x + 166. The x-coordinates of P, 2P, 4P, 8P for P = (3, 8) \
are 3, -5, 11, 3, and #E(F_3) = 7, so E(Q)_tors is cyclic of order 7.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"805ff50e-7ab9-4de4-b4f9-df46b9df808d"],

