Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Exercise 10.19", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"59bbb283-a5dc-449f-9a1b-eb8161dc0876"],

Cell["\<\
y^2 = x^3 + D (j = 0). (b) If p = 2 mod 3 then #E(F_p) = p + 1. (d) E(Q)_tors \
is Z/6 for D = 1, Z/3 if D != 1 is a square or D = -432, Z/2 if D != 1 is a \
cube, and trivial otherwise. (The copy of the book I read has the words \
square and cube interchanged in (d); the computation below follows the \
correct statement.)\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"77c0ec4d-e491-4e89-8d93-096d7f315ed6"],

